IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 12, Division 3 (insider trading), third part: ss 222 to 231 (exceptions, attribution of knowledge, parity of information defences).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Reading an answer and the markers are explained at the head of sfab-division-1.l4 and in NOTES.md.
-- Direction of each answer. A function named "the exception applies" or "does not apply" answers JUST TRUE where the exception relieves the case.
-- Where the text says the section "does not apply in respect of X", an unmet X answers NOTHING (limited by its own wording).
-- Where the text says a person "does not contravene ... if (a), (b) and (c)", a failed "if" answers JUST FALSE (the section gives no relief on these facts;
-- MARGINAL-READING (a)); the defences of s 231 do the same under the Guide's ruling on defences of 2026-11-05, (b).

§ `s 222: exception for redemption of units in a collective investment scheme`

-- src:35540 | 222. Sections 218(2) and 219(2) do not apply in respect of the
-- src:35541 | redemption of units in a collective investment scheme by a trustee or
-- src:35542 | manager under a trust deed relating to that collective investment
-- src:35543 | scheme in accordance with a buy‑back covenant contained or deemed
-- src:35544 | to be contained in the trust deed at a price that is required by the trust
-- src:35545 | deed to be calculated, so far as is reasonably practicable, by reference
-- src:35546 | to the underlying value of the assets less —
-- src:35548 | (a) any liabilities of that collective investment scheme to
-- src:35549 | which the units relates; and
-- src:35551 | (b) any reasonable charge for purchasing the units.
@ref s 222 (src:35540-35551)
GIVEN
    `the act is the redemption of units in a collective investment scheme by a trustee or manager under a trust deed relating to the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act the redemption of units in a collective investment scheme by a trustee or manager under a trust deed relating to that scheme?
    `the redemption is in accordance with a buy-back covenant contained or deemed to be contained in the trust deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the redemption in accordance with a buy-back covenant contained or deemed to be contained in the trust deed?
    `the price is required by the trust deed to be calculated, so far as is reasonably practicable, by reference to the underlying value of the assets less the liabilities of the scheme to which the units relate and any reasonable charge for purchasing the units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the price one that the trust deed requires to be calculated, so far as is reasonably practicable, by reference to the underlying value of the assets less (a) any liabilities of the scheme to which the units relate and (b) any reasonable charge for purchasing the units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222 sections 218(2) and 219(2) do not apply to the redemption of units` MEANS
    IF `the act is the redemption of units in a collective investment scheme by a trustee or manager under a trust deed relating to the scheme` AND `the redemption is in accordance with a buy-back covenant contained or deemed to be contained in the trust deed` AND `the price is required by the trust deed to be calculated, so far as is reasonably practicable, by reference to the underlying value of the assets less the liabilities of the scheme to which the units relate and any reasonable charge for purchasing the units`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 218(2) and 219(2) do not apply in respect of the redemption of units in a collective investment scheme"

§ `s 223: exception for underwriters`

-- src:35558 | 223.—(1) Sections 218(2) and 219(2) do not apply in respect of —
-- src:35560 | (a) subscribing for, or purchasing, securities, securities‑based
-- src:35561 | derivatives contracts or CIS units under an underwriting
-- src:35562 | agreement or a sub‑underwriting agreement;
-- src:35564 | (b) entering into an agreement referred to in paragraph (a); or
-- src:35566 | (c) selling securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or
-- src:35567 | CIS units subscribed for, or purchased, under an agreement
-- src:35568 | referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref s 223(1) (src:35558-35568)
GIVEN
    `the act is subscribing for, or purchasing, securities, contracts or units under an underwriting agreement or a sub-underwriting agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act subscribing for, or purchasing, securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units under an underwriting agreement or a sub-underwriting agreement?
    `the act is entering into an underwriting agreement or a sub-underwriting agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act entering into an agreement referred to in section 223(1)(a)?
    `the act is selling securities, contracts or units subscribed for or purchased under an underwriting agreement or a sub-underwriting agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act selling securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units subscribed for, or purchased, under an agreement referred to in section 223(1)(a)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223(1) sections 218(2) and 219(2) do not apply to the underwriting act` MEANS
    IF `the act is subscribing for, or purchasing, securities, contracts or units under an underwriting agreement or a sub-underwriting agreement` OR `the act is entering into an underwriting agreement or a sub-underwriting agreement` OR `the act is selling securities, contracts or units subscribed for or purchased under an underwriting agreement or a sub-underwriting agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 218(2) and 219(2) do not apply in respect of"

-- src:35572 | (2) Sections 218(3) and 219(3) do not apply in respect of the
-- src:35573 | communication of information in relation to securities,
-- src:35574 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units —
-- src:35576 | (a) to a person solely for the purpose of procuring the person to
-- src:35577 | enter into an underwriting agreement in relation to any
-- src:35578 | such securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or
-- src:35579 | CIS units; or
-- src:35581 | (b) by a person who may be required under an underwriting
-- src:35582 | agreement to subscribe for, or purchase, any such
-- src:35583 | securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS
-- src:35584 | units if the communication is made to another person
-- src:35585 | solely for the purpose of procuring the other person to do
-- src:35586 | either or both of the following:
-- src:35588 | (i) enter into a sub‑underwriting agreement in relation
-- src:35589 | to any such securities, securities‑based derivatives
-- src:35590 | contracts or CIS units;
-- src:35592 | (ii) subscribe for, or purchase, any such securities,
-- src:35593 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units.
@ref s 223(2) (src:35572-35593)
GIVEN
    `the communication is to a person solely for the purpose of procuring the person to enter into an underwriting agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication of information in relation to the securities, contracts or units made to a person solely for the purpose of procuring the person to enter into an underwriting agreement in relation to them?
    `the communication is by a person who may be required under an underwriting agreement to subscribe for or purchase the securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication made by a person who may be required under an underwriting agreement to subscribe for, or purchase, the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units?
    `the communication is made to another person solely for the purpose of procuring the other person to enter into a sub-underwriting agreement or to subscribe for or purchase them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication made to another person solely for the purpose of procuring the other person to enter into a sub-underwriting agreement in relation to them, or to subscribe for, or purchase, them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223(2) sections 218(3) and 219(3) do not apply to the underwriting communication` MEANS
    IF `the communication is to a person solely for the purpose of procuring the person to enter into an underwriting agreement` OR (`the communication is by a person who may be required under an underwriting agreement to subscribe for or purchase the securities, contracts or units` AND `the communication is made to another person solely for the purpose of procuring the other person to enter into a sub-underwriting agreement or to subscribe for or purchase them`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 218(3) and 219(3) do not apply in respect of the communication of information"

§ `s 224: exception for purchase pursuant to legal requirement`

