§ `s 226: attribution of knowledge within corporations`

-- src:35628 | 226.—(1) For the purposes of this Division —
-- src:35630 | (a) a corporation is taken to possess any information which an
-- src:35631 | officer of the corporation possesses and which came into
-- src:35632 | his or her possession in the course of the performance of
-- src:35633 | duties as such an officer; and
@ref s 226(1)(a) (src:35628-35633)
GIVEN
    `an officer of the corporation possesses the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an officer of the corporation possess the information?
    `the information came into the officer's possession in the course of the performance of duties as such an officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the information come into the officer's possession in the course of the performance of duties as such an officer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226(1)(a) the corporation is taken to possess the information that its officer possesses` MEANS
    IF `an officer of the corporation possesses the information` AND `the information came into the officer's possession in the course of the performance of duties as such an officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which an officer of the corporation possesses and which came into his or her possession in the course of the performance of duties as such an officer"

-- src:35635 | (b) if an officer of a corporation knows or ought reasonably to
-- src:35636 | know any matter or thing because he or she is an officer of
-- src:35637 | the corporation, it is to be presumed, until the contrary is
-- src:35638 | proved, that the corporation knows or ought reasonably to
-- src:35639 | know that matter or thing.
@ref s 226(1)(b) (src:35635-35639)
GIVEN
    `an officer of the corporation knows or ought reasonably to know a matter or thing because the officer is an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an officer of the corporation know, or ought the officer reasonably to know, a matter or thing because he or she is an officer of the corporation?
    `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226(1)(b) the corporation is presumed to know or ought reasonably to know the matter or thing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an officer of the corporation knows or ought reasonably to know a matter or thing because the officer is an officer of the corporation`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if an officer of a corporation knows or ought reasonably to know any matter or thing because he or she is an officer of the corporation"
        IF `the contrary is proved`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is to be presumed, until the contrary is proved"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:35641 | (2) A corporation does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by
-- src:35642 | entering into a transaction or agreement at any time merely because of
-- src:35643 | information in the possession of an officer of the corporation if —
-- src:35645 | (a) the decision to enter into the transaction or agreement was
-- src:35646 | taken on its behalf by a person other than that officer;
-- src:35648 | (b) it had in operation at that time arrangements that could
-- src:35649 | reasonably be expected to ensure that the information was
-- src:35650 | not communicated to the person who made the decision
-- src:35651 | and that no advice with respect to the transaction or
-- src:35656 | agreement was given to that person by a person in
-- src:35657 | possession of the information; and
-- src:35659 | (c) the information was not so communicated and no such
-- src:35660 | advice was so given.
@ref s 226(2) (src:35641-35660)
GIVEN
    `the corporation entered into the transaction or agreement merely because of information in the possession of an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation enter into the transaction or agreement merely because of information in the possession of an officer of the corporation?
    `the decision to enter into the transaction or agreement was taken on the corporation's behalf by a person other than that officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision to enter into the transaction or agreement taken on the corporation's behalf by a person other than that officer?
    `the corporation had in operation at that time arrangements that could reasonably be expected to ensure that the information was not communicated to the decision-maker and that no advice was given by a person in possession of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation have in operation at that time arrangements that could reasonably be expected to ensure that the information was not communicated to the person who made the decision, and that no advice with respect to the transaction or agreement was given to that person by a person in possession of the information?
    `the information was not so communicated and no such advice was so given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information not so communicated, and was no such advice so given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 226(2) the corporation does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by reason of its officer's information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the corporation entered into the transaction or agreement merely because of information in the possession of an officer of the corporation`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "merely because of information in the possession of an officer of the corporation"
        IF `the decision to enter into the transaction or agreement was taken on the corporation's behalf by a person other than that officer` AND `the corporation had in operation at that time arrangements that could reasonably be expected to ensure that the information was not communicated to the decision-maker and that no advice was given by a person in possession of it` AND `the information was not so communicated and no such advice was so given`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by entering into a transaction or agreement at any time merely because of information in the possession of an officer of the corporation if" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

§ `s 227: attribution of knowledge within partnerships and limited liability partnerships`

-- src:35665 | 227.—(1) For the purposes of this Division —
-- src:35667 | (a) a partner of a partnership or a limited liability partnership
-- src:35668 | (as the case may be) is taken to possess any information —
-- src:35670 | (i) which another partner of the partnership or limited
-- src:35671 | liability partnership (as the case may be) possesses
-- src:35672 | and which came into such other partner’s possession
-- src:35673 | in his or her capacity as a partner of the partnership or
-- src:35674 | limited liability partnership (as the case may be); or
-- src:35676 | (ii) which an employee of the partnership or a manager
-- src:35677 | of a limited liability partnership (as the case may be)
-- src:35678 | possesses and which came into the possession of
-- src:35679 | such an employee or manager in the course of the
-- src:35680 | performance of his or her duties as such an employee
-- src:35681 | or manager; and
@ref s 227(1)(a) (src:35665-35681)
GIVEN
    `another partner possesses the information and it came into that partner's possession in the capacity as a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another partner of the partnership or limited liability partnership possess the information, and did it come into that partner's possession in his or her capacity as a partner?
    `an employee of the partnership or a manager of the limited liability partnership possesses the information and it came into that person's possession in the course of the performance of duties as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an employee of the partnership, or a manager of the limited liability partnership, possess the information, and did it come into that person's possession in the course of the performance of his or her duties as such an employee or manager?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(1)(a) the partner is taken to possess the information that another partner, an employee or a manager possesses` MEANS
    IF `another partner possesses the information and it came into that partner's possession in the capacity as a partner` OR `an employee of the partnership or a manager of the limited liability partnership possesses the information and it came into that person's possession in the course of the performance of duties as such`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a partner of a partnership or a limited liability partnership (as the case may be) is taken to possess any information"

-- src:35683 | (b) if a partner or employee of a partnership or a partner,
-- src:35684 | manager or employee of a limited liability partnership (as
-- src:35685 | the case may be) knows or ought reasonably to know any
-- src:35686 | matter or thing in his or her capacity as such a partner,
-- src:35687 | manager or employee, it is to be presumed that every
-- src:35688 | partner of the partnership or limited liability partnership
-- src:35689 | (as the case may be) knows or ought reasonably to know
-- src:35690 | that matter or thing.
@ref s 227(1)(b) (src:35683-35690)
GIVEN
    `a partner or employee of a partnership, or a partner, manager or employee of a limited liability partnership, knows or ought reasonably to know a matter or thing in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a partner or employee of a partnership, or a partner, manager or employee of a limited liability partnership, know or ought he or she reasonably to know a matter or thing in his or her capacity as such a partner, manager or employee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(1)(b) every partner is presumed to know or ought reasonably to know the matter or thing` MEANS
    IF `a partner or employee of a partnership, or a partner, manager or employee of a limited liability partnership, knows or ought reasonably to know a matter or thing in that capacity`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says "it is to be presumed" and names no way to rebut it; none is invented (NOTES.md fork F-227)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "knows or ought reasonably to know any matter or thing in his or her capacity as such a partner, manager or employee"

-- src:35692 | (2) The partners of a partnership or limited liability partnership (as
-- src:35693 | the case may be) do not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by
-- src:35694 | entering into a transaction or agreement at any time merely because
-- src:35695 | one or more (but not all) of the partners, or a manager or managers, or
-- src:35696 | an employee or employees, of the partnership or limited liability
-- src:35701 | partnership (as the case may be) are in actual possession of
-- src:35702 | information if —
-- src:35704 | (a) the decision to enter into the transaction or agreement was
-- src:35705 | taken on behalf of the partnership or limited liability
-- src:35706 | partnership by any one or more of the following persons:
-- src:35708 | (i) a partner who is taken to have possessed the
-- src:35709 | information merely because another partner, or a
-- src:35710 | manager or employee, of the partnership or limited
-- src:35711 | liability partnership, was in possession of the
-- src:35712 | information;
-- src:35714 | (ii) an employee of the partnership or limited liability
-- src:35715 | partnership or a manager of the limited liability
-- src:35716 | partnership who was not in possession of the
-- src:35717 | information;
-- src:35719 | (b) the partnership or limited liability partnership had in
-- src:35720 | operation at that time arrangements that could reasonably
-- src:35721 | be expected to ensure that the information was not
-- src:35722 | communicated to the person or persons who made the
-- src:35723 | decision and that no advice with respect to the transaction
-- src:35724 | or agreement was given to that person or any of those
-- src:35725 | persons by a person in possession of the information; and
-- src:35727 | (c) the information was not so communicated and no such
-- src:35728 | advice was so given.
@ref s 227(2) (src:35692-35728)
GIVEN
    `the partners entered into the transaction or agreement merely because one or more but not all of the partners, managers or employees are in actual possession of the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the partners enter into the transaction or agreement merely because one or more (but not all) of the partners, or a manager or managers, or an employee or employees, of the partnership or limited liability partnership are in actual possession of information?
    `the decision was taken by a partner who is taken to have possessed the information merely because another partner, a manager or an employee was in possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision to enter into the transaction or agreement taken by a partner who is taken to have possessed the information merely because another partner, or a manager or employee, was in possession of it?
    `the decision was taken by an employee of the partnership or a manager of the limited liability partnership who was not in possession of the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision taken by an employee of the partnership or limited liability partnership, or a manager of the limited liability partnership, who was not in possession of the information?
    `the partnership had in operation at that time arrangements that could reasonably be expected to ensure that the information was not communicated to the decision-maker and that no advice was given by a person in possession of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the partnership or limited liability partnership have in operation at that time arrangements that could reasonably be expected to ensure that the information was not communicated to the person or persons who made the decision, and that no advice with respect to the transaction or agreement was given to that person or any of those persons by a person in possession of the information?
    `the information was not so communicated and no such advice was so given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information not so communicated, and was no such advice so given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(2) the partners do not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by reason of one partner's, manager's or employee's information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the partners entered into the transaction or agreement merely because one or more but not all of the partners, managers or employees are in actual possession of the information`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "merely because one or more (but not all) of the partners"
        IF (`the decision was taken by a partner who is taken to have possessed the information merely because another partner, a manager or an employee was in possession` OR `the decision was taken by an employee of the partnership or a manager of the limited liability partnership who was not in possession of the information`) AND `the partnership had in operation at that time arrangements that could reasonably be expected to ensure that the information was not communicated to the decision-maker and that no advice was given by a person in possession of it` AND `the information was not so communicated and no such advice was so given`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by entering into a transaction or agreement at any time merely because one or more" "are in actual possession of information if" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- src:35730 | (3) A partner of a partnership or limited liability partnership (as the
-- src:35731 | case may be) does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by
-- src:35732 | entering into a transaction or agreement otherwise than on behalf of
-- src:35733 | the partnership or limited liability partnership merely because he or
-- src:35734 | she is taken to possess information that is in the possession of another
-- src:35735 | partner, a manager or an employee of the partnership.
@ref s 227(3) (src:35730-35735)
GIVEN
    `the partner entered into the transaction or agreement otherwise than on behalf of the partnership or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the partner enter into the transaction or agreement otherwise than on behalf of the partnership or limited liability partnership?
    `the partner is taken to possess information that is in the possession of another partner, a manager or an employee of the partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the partner taken to possess information that is in the possession of another partner, a manager or an employee of the partnership or limited liability partnership?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 227(3) the partner does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) merely because the partner is taken to possess the information` MEANS
    IF `the partner entered into the transaction or agreement otherwise than on behalf of the partnership or limited liability partnership` AND `the partner is taken to possess information that is in the possession of another partner, a manager or an employee of the partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by entering into a transaction or agreement otherwise than on behalf of the partnership or limited liability partnership merely because he or she is taken to possess information"

§ `s 228: exception for knowledge of an individual's own intentions or activities`

-- src:35740 | 228. An individual does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by
-- src:35741 | entering into a transaction or agreement in relation to securities,
-- src:35742 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units merely because the
-- src:35747 | individual is aware that the individual proposes to enter into, or has
-- src:35748 | previously entered into, one or more transactions or agreements in
-- src:35749 | relation to those securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or
-- src:35750 | CIS units.
@ref s 228 (src:35740-35750)
GIVEN
    `the individual entered into the transaction or agreement merely because the individual is aware that the individual proposes to enter into, or has previously entered into, transactions or agreements in relation to those securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the individual enter into the transaction or agreement in relation to securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units merely because the individual is aware that the individual proposes to enter into, or has previously entered into, one or more transactions or agreements in relation to those securities, contracts or units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228 the individual does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) merely because the individual is aware of the individual's own intentions or activities` MEANS
    IF `the individual entered into the transaction or agreement merely because the individual is aware that the individual proposes to enter into, or has previously entered into, transactions or agreements in relation to those securities, contracts or units`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by entering into a transaction or agreement in relation to securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units merely because"

§ `s 229: exception for corporations and their officers`

-- src:35756 | 229.—(1) A corporation does not contravene section 218(2) or
-- src:35757 | 219(2) by entering into a transaction or agreement in relation to
-- src:35758 | securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units merely
-- src:35759 | because the corporation is aware that it proposes to enter into or has
-- src:35760 | previously entered into, one or more transactions or agreements in
-- src:35761 | relation to those securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or
