@ref s 229(1) (src:35756-35762)
GIVEN
    `the corporation entered into the transaction or agreement merely because the corporation is aware that it proposes to enter into, or has previously entered into, transactions or agreements in relation to those securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation enter into the transaction or agreement merely because the corporation is aware that it proposes to enter into, or has previously entered into, one or more transactions or agreements in relation to those securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 229(1) the corporation does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) merely because the corporation is aware of its own intentions or activities` MEANS
    IF `the corporation entered into the transaction or agreement merely because the corporation is aware that it proposes to enter into, or has previously entered into, transactions or agreements in relation to those securities, contracts or units`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by entering into a transaction or agreement in relation to securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units merely because the corporation is aware"

