§ `s 230: unsolicited transactions by the holder of a capital markets services licence and representatives`

-- src:35804 | 230.—(1) The holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in
-- src:35805 | capital markets products, or a representative of such a holder, does
-- src:35806 | not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by subscribing for,
-- src:35807 | purchasing or selling, or entering into an agreement to subscribe
-- src:35808 | for, purchase or sell, securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:35809 | or CIS units if —
-- src:35811 | (a) the holder or representative entered into the transaction or
-- src:35812 | agreement concerned on behalf of another person (called in
-- src:35813 | this section the principal) under a specific instruction by
-- src:35814 | the principal to enter into that transaction or agreement
-- src:35815 | which was not solicited by the holder or representative;
-- src:35817 | (b) the holder or representative has not given any advice to the
-- src:35818 | principal in relation to the transaction or agreement or
-- src:35819 | otherwise sought to procure the principal’s instructions to
-- src:35820 | enter into the transaction or agreement; and
-- src:35822 | (c) the principal is not an associate of the holder or
-- src:35823 | representative.
@ref s 230(1) (src:35804-35823)
GIVEN
    `the person is the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products, or a representative of such a holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products, or a representative of such a holder?
    `the holder or representative entered into the transaction on behalf of the principal under a specific instruction by the principal that was not solicited by the holder or representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the holder or representative enter into the transaction or agreement on behalf of another person (the principal) under a specific instruction by the principal to enter into that transaction or agreement which was not solicited by the holder or representative?
    `the holder or representative has not given advice to the principal in relation to the transaction or otherwise sought to procure the principal's instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the holder or representative not given any advice to the principal in relation to the transaction or agreement, or otherwise sought to procure the principal's instructions to enter into it?
    `the principal is an associate of the holder or representative (as section 3 reads)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the principal an associate of the holder or representative? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 3(1), or NOTHING if not known)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 230(1) the holder or representative does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by an unsolicited transaction for a principal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products, or a representative of such a holder`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products, or a representative of such a holder"
        IF (NOT `the holder or representative entered into the transaction on behalf of the principal under a specific instruction by the principal that was not solicited by the holder or representative`) OR (NOT `the holder or representative has not given advice to the principal in relation to the transaction or otherwise sought to procure the principal's instructions`) OR (`the principal is an associate of the holder or representative (as section 3 reads)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by subscribing for, purchasing or selling" "if" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        IF `the principal is an associate of the holder or representative (as section 3 reads)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the principal is an associate was not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:35827 | (2) Nothing in this section affects the application of section 218(2)
-- src:35828 | or 219(2) in relation to the principal.
@ref s 230(2) (src:35827-35828)
GIVEN
    `the person is the principal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the principal on whose behalf the holder or representative entered into the transaction or agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 230(2) section 230 does not affect the application of sections 218(2) and 219(2) to the principal` MEANS
    IF `the person is the principal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to the principal"

§ `s 231: parity of information defences`

-- src:35832 | 231.—(1) In any proceedings against a person for a contravention
-- src:35833 | of section 218(2) or 219(2) because the person entered into, or
-- src:35834 | procured another person to enter into, a transaction or agreement at a
-- src:35835 | time when certain information was in the firstmentioned person’s
-- src:35836 | possession, it is a defence if the court is satisfied that —
-- src:35838 | (a) the information came into the firstmentioned person’s
-- src:35839 | possession solely as a result of the information having been
-- src:35840 | made known as referred to in section 215(b)(i); or
-- src:35845 | (b) the other party to the transaction or agreement knew, or
-- src:35846 | ought reasonably to have known, of the information before
-- src:35847 | entering into the transaction or agreement.
@ref s 231(1) (src:35832-35847)
GIVEN
    `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218(2) or 219(2) because the person entered into, or procured another person to enter into, a transaction or agreement at a time when certain information was in the person's possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for a contravention of section 218(2) or 219(2) because the person entered into, or procured another person to enter into, a transaction or agreement at a time when certain information was in the person's possession?
    `the information came into the person's possession solely as a result of its having been made known as referred to in section 215(b)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the information came into the person's possession solely as a result of the information having been made known as referred to in section 215(b)(i)?
    `the other party to the transaction or agreement knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the information before entering into it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the other party to the transaction or agreement knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the information before entering into the transaction or agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(1) the person has the parity of information defence to the contravention by dealing or procuring` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218(2) or 219(2) because the person entered into, or procured another person to enter into, a transaction or agreement at a time when certain information was in the person's possession`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings against a person for a contravention of section 218(2) or 219(2) because the person entered into"
        IF `the information came into the person's possession solely as a result of its having been made known as referred to in section 215(b)(i)` OR `the other party to the transaction or agreement knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the information before entering into it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence if the court is satisfied that" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [DEFENCE]

-- src:35849 | (2) In an action against a person for a contravention of
-- src:35850 | section 218(3) or 219(3) because the person communicated
-- src:35851 | information, or caused information to be communicated, to another
-- src:35852 | person, it is a defence if the court is satisfied that —
-- src:35854 | (a) the information came into the firstmentioned person’s
-- src:35855 | possession solely as a result of the information having been
-- src:35856 | made known as referred in section 215(b)(i); or
-- src:35858 | (b) the other person knew, or ought reasonably to have known,
-- src:35859 | of the information before the information was
-- src:35860 | communicated.
@ref s 231(2) (src:35849-35860)
GIVEN
    `the action is for a contravention of section 218(3) or 219(3) because the person communicated information, or caused information to be communicated, to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action against the person for a contravention of section 218(3) or 219(3) because the person communicated information, or caused information to be communicated, to another person?
    `the information came into the person's possession solely as a result of its having been made known as referred to in section 215(b)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the information came into the person's possession solely as a result of the information having been made known as referred to in section 215(b)(i)?
    `the other person knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the information before it was communicated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the other person knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the information before the information was communicated?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(2) the person has the parity of information defence to the contravention by communicating` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is for a contravention of section 218(3) or 219(3) because the person communicated information, or caused information to be communicated, to another person`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In an action against a person for a contravention of section 218(3) or 219(3) because the person communicated information"
        IF `the information came into the person's possession solely as a result of its having been made known as referred to in section 215(b)(i)` OR `the other person knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the information before it was communicated`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence if the court is satisfied that" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [DEFENCE]
